1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,293
Hello, I'm delighted to welcome you to our Wildlife Club,

2
00:00:03,293 --> 00:00:06,280
and very pleased that you're interested in the countryside

3
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:08,890
and the plants and creatures of this area.

4
00:00:08,890 --> 00:00:13,040
I think you'll be surprised at the variety we have here

5
00:00:13,040 --> 00:00:14,900
even though we're not far from London.

6
00:00:14,900 --> 00:00:20,090
I'll start by telling you about some of the parks and open spaces nearby.

7
00:00:20,090 --> 00:00:24,050
One very pleasant place is Halland Common.

8
00:00:24,050 --> 00:00:27,820
This has been public land for hundreds of years

9
00:00:28,120 --> 00:00:31,374
and what you'll find interesting is that the River Ouse,

10
00:00:31,374 --> 00:00:36,770
which flows into the sea eighty kilometres away, has its source in the common.

11
00:00:36,770 --> 00:00:41,512
There's an information board about the plants and animals you can see here,

12
00:00:41,512 --> 00:00:45,890
and by the way, the common is accessible 24 hours a day.

13
00:00:45,890 --> 00:00:51,670
Then there's Holt Island, which is noted for its great range of trees.

14
00:00:51,670 --> 00:00:56,770
In the past willows were grown here commercially for basket-making,

15
00:00:56,770 --> 00:01:00,850
and this ancient craft has recently been reintroduced.

16
00:01:00,850 --> 00:01:04,996
The island is only open to the public from Friday to Sunday,

17
00:01:04,996 --> 00:01:09,360
because it's quite small, and if there were people around every day

18
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:11,560
much of the wildlife would keep away.

19
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:17,410
From there it's just a short walk across the bridge to Longfield Country Park.

20
00:01:17,410 --> 00:01:23,000
Longfield has a modern replica of a farm from over two thousand years ago.

21
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:29,340
Children's activities are often arranged there, like bread-making and face-painting.

22
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:33,040
The park is only open during daylight hours

23
00:01:33,180 --> 00:01:35,680
so bear that in mind if you decide to go there.

24
00:01:35,680 --> 00:01:39,284
Longfield Park has a programme of activities throughout the year,

25
00:01:39,284 --> 00:01:44,690
and to give you a sample, this is what's happening in the next few days.

26
00:01:44,690 --> 00:01:50,710
On Monday you can learn about herbs, and how they've been used over the centuries.

27
00:01:50,710 --> 00:01:58,160
You'll start with a tour of our herb garden, practise the technique of using them as colour dyes for cloth.

28
00:01:58,160 --> 00:02:03,360
And listen to an illustrated talk about their use in cooking and medicine.

29
00:02:03,360 --> 00:02:09,173
Then on Wednesday you can join local experts to discover the variety of insects

30
00:02:09,173 --> 00:02:12,080
and birds that appear in the evening.

31
00:02:12,080 --> 00:02:15,518
We keep to a small number of people in the group,

32
00:02:15,518 --> 00:02:20,830
so if you want to go you'll need to phone the park ranger a few days ahead.

33
00:02:20,830 --> 00:02:24,160
There's a small charge, which you should pay when you turn up.

34
00:02:24,160 --> 00:02:30,381
I'm sure you're all keen to help with the practical task of looking after the park,

35
00:02:30,381 --> 00:02:33,880
so on Saturday you can join a working party.

36
00:02:33,880 --> 00:02:37,000
You'll have a choice of all sorts of activities

37
00:02:37,220 --> 00:02:39,077
from planting hedges to picking up litter

38
00:02:39,077 --> 00:02:43,950
so you'll be able to change from one to another when you feel like it.

39
00:02:43,950 --> 00:02:47,640
The rangers will be hard at work all day

40
00:02:47,660 --> 00:02:51,100
but do come and join in, even for just a short while.

41
00:02:51,100 --> 00:02:57,730
One thing, though, is to make sure you're wearing something that you don't mind getting dirty or torn.

42
00:02:57,730 --> 00:03:02,869
And finally I'd like to tell you about our new wildlife area,

43
00:03:02,869 --> 00:03:07,580
Hinchingbrooke Park, which will be opened to the public next month.

44
00:03:07,580 --> 00:03:11,041
This slide doesn't really indicate how big it is,

45
00:03:11,041 --> 00:03:16,810
but anyway, you can see the two gates into the park, and the main paths.

46
00:03:16,810 --> 00:03:20,484
As you can see, there's a lake in the north west of the park,

47
00:03:20,484 --> 00:03:24,420
with a bird hide to the west of it, at the end of a path.

48
00:03:24,420 --> 00:03:28,750
So it'll be a nice quiet place for watching the birds on the lake.

49
00:03:28,750 --> 00:03:31,580
Fairly close to where refreshments are available,

50
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:36,420
there's a dog-walking area in the southern part of the park

51
00:03:36,420 --> 00:03:38,050
leading off from the path.

52
00:03:38,050 --> 00:03:43,625
And if you just want to sit and relax, you can go to the flower garden;

53
00:03:43,625 --> 00:03:47,110
that's the circular area on the map surrounded by paths.

54
00:03:47,110 --> 00:03:53,600
And finally, there's a wooded area in the western section of the park, between two paths.

55
00:03:53,600 --> 00:03:57,400
Okay, that's enough from me, so let's go on to...
